From: Joel Winarske <joel.winarske@linux.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Forward HOME when downloading external sources

download_external_sources() runs its nested CMake through `env -i` with only
PATH preserved. build_external_dependencies(), a hundred lines below, does the
same but also forwards HOME -- so the two disagree about what a sub-build needs.

On macOS the download step reaches CocoaPods, which invokes brew, which refuses
to run without HOME:

    Error: $HOME must be set to run brew.

The failure is not fatal on its own, so the build continues and dies later
somewhere unrelated. Linux does not notice because nothing in the download step
shells out to a tool that needs a home directory.

Forward HOME in both places, matching what the build function already does.

--- a/cmake/external_rules.cmake
+++ b/cmake/external_rules.cmake
@@ -26,7 +26,8 @@ function(download_external_sources)
     set(ENV_COMMAND "")
   else()
     set(firebase_command_line_path "$ENV{PATH}")
-    set(ENV_COMMAND env -i PATH=${firebase_command_line_path})
+    set(firebase_command_line_home "$ENV{HOME}")
+    set(ENV_COMMAND env -i PATH=${firebase_command_line_path} HOME=${firebase_command_line_home})
   endif()
 
   if(IOS)
